From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tiago Medicci <tiago.medicci@espressif.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 19:30:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] configure: look up meson from PATH

OpenEmbedded provides a compatible meson-native and a wrapper that adds
the correct nativesdk cross and native files. Use it instead of requiring
QEMU's private virtual environment.

This follows the equivalent OpenEmbedded-Core QEMU workaround.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [OpenEmbedded-specific]
Signed-off-by: Tiago Medicci <tiago.medicci@espressif.com>
---
 configure | 11 ++++-------
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/configure b/configure
index b12ee2133b..3ea8cce38b 100755
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -1002,10 +1002,8 @@ $mkvenv ensuregroup --dir "${source_path}/python/wheels" \
      ${source_path}/pythondeps.toml meson || exit 1
 
-# At this point, we expect Meson to be installed and available.
-# We expect mkvenv or pip to have created pyvenv/bin/meson for us.
-# We ignore PATH completely here: we want to use the venv's Meson
-# *exclusively*.
-
-meson="$(cd pyvenv/bin; pwd)/meson"
+meson="$(command -v meson)"
+if test -z "$meson"; then
+    error_exit "meson not found in PATH"
+fi
 
 # Conditionally ensure Sphinx is installed.
